const content="<article data-editorial-version=\"3\" class=\"sn-page\"><div class=\"sn-read\"><a href=\"/supporters/\">← Featured sponsors</a><p class=\"sn-kicker\">Marine Diesel Engine · Sponsor feature</p><img class=\"sn-logo\" src=\"/images/supporters/ferosticker/logo.webp\" alt=\"FeroSticker logo\" width=\"210\" height=\"100\"><h1>FeroSticker: automatic suppression for fires in suitable small compartments</h1><p class=\"sn-intro\">FeroSticker makes compact heat-activated devices that release fire-suppressing aerosol into suitable enclosed spaces. The units work without batteries or an electrical connection, providing an automatic local response in the compartment they are selected to protect.</p><img class=\"sn-hero\" src=\"/images/supporters/ferosticker/f01.webp\" alt=\"FeroSticker F01 device and packaging\" width=\"1200\" height=\"1200\"><section><h2>A device that responds to heat</h2><p>The published activation temperature is approximately 170°C at the unit. Once activated, it releases aerosol without a person pressing a switch or a powered controller directing the response.</p><p>We like that independence from the boat&#x27;s supply. It is a useful characteristic for equipment intended to operate during a fire, and its purpose is simple to understand: suppression within an appropriate enclosed volume.</p></section><section><h2>Size the application correctly</h2><p>F01, F03 and F09 models cover different enclosure volumes. The space, internal divisions and installation requirements need to be assessed together. The compact format is useful where room is limited, but correct application is what gives the device its role.</p><p>For owners reviewing machinery and equipment areas, that means considering specific suitable compartments rather than treating the product as a whole-vessel solution. The manufacturer’s enclosure requirements provide the basis for the selection.</p></section><section><h2>Why we feature FeroSticker</h2><p>Looking after a boat includes equipment that may never be called on during an ordinary outing. We feature FeroSticker because its automatic activation addresses a developing fire that may be hidden from the crew.</p><p>Heat activation, compact dimensions and no reliance on electricity are practical reasons to investigate it. The product offers a defined kind of protection for suitable enclosed spaces, with model choice and installation tied to the actual compartment aboard.</p></section><div class=\"sn-contact\"><a href=\"https://ferosticker.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"sponsored nofollow noopener noreferrer\">Discover FeroSticker ↗</a><a href=\"/supporters/\">More featured sponsors</a></div></div></article><script type=\"application/ld+json\">{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\", \"@type\": \"Article\", \"headline\": \"FeroSticker: automatic suppression for fires in suitable small compartments\", \"description\": \"FeroSticker offers automatic fire suppression for suitable enclosed boat compartments, activated by heat without batteries or onboard power.\", \"image\": \"https://marinedieselengine.com.au/images/supporters/ferosticker/f01.webp\", \"author\": {\"@type\": \"Organization\", \"name\": \"Marine Diesel Engine\"}, \"dateModified\": \"2026-11-05\", \"mainEntityOfPage\": \"https://marinedieselengine.com.au/supporters/ferosticker/\"}</script>";
